 "notes": "All 7 old kinds kept (Czech premium pale lager renamed Czech pale lager); 3 new kinds added (Dortmunder Export, Kellerbier, Festbier). Old homebrew/craft models kept in m. Commercial examples taken from BJCP 2021 pages and Wikipedia; makers in m are the brewery brand names. Left out: Negra Modelo as a Vienna archetype (Wikipedia calls it Dunkel-style; Victoria used instead); Samuel Adams Boston Lager (page calls it only 'amber lager'); Singha, Red Stripe, Foster's etc. (maker not on a retrieved page); Kellerbier commercial examples (none named on retrieved pages); Wikipedia 'Oktoberfest_beer' page 404. Augustiner Oktoberfest placed in Festbier per BJCP 2021 although Wikipedia calls it a Märzen. No craft tradition entries (industrial styles)."
